Improved Toggle Coverage Reporting for Structures
When reporting toggle coverage for a signal of a structure type, VCS by default uses the
location where the structure type was declared. When multiple signals are declared with
that type, it becomes difficult to identify which signal is being reported.
Now, VCS allows you to see the location where the signal of structure type was declared
instead of where the structure type itself was declared. For this, no additional switch is
required at compile time.
Consider Example 7 that shows the definitions of two structures, mst1 and mst2. The
example also shows the mst2 structure with two instances, stVar1 and stVar2.
Example 7 structs.v
