m, "bins b1 = arr;"
Currently support for set covergroup expressions is available
under VCS compile time switch
'-covg_enable_sce'.
• URG Report

Consider the following code snippet that shows an array of 3 values, arr, to define the
range of bin b1:
int arr[3];
int x;

cp1 : coverpoint x {
bins b1[3] = arr ;
}
cg cginst;

arr[0] = 27;
arr[1] = 41;
arr[2] = 58;
cginst = new;
x = 41;
#2 cginst.sample();
#2 $finish;
end
In this example, the arr array is initialized to contain the three values 27, 41, and 58.
When the -covg_enable_sce switch is used at compile time, three separate bins are
created with values 27, 41, and 58 respectively.
Figure 19 shows the three separate bins, b1[27], b1[41], and b1[58] in a URG report.

Coverage Support for Inconsequential Code Reduction
Figure 19 URG Report
• Functions with return type as array are not supported.
• A single bin can include up to 131071 ranges or values, whether specified directly or
through an array. If the number of ranges or values exceeds this limit (for example,
131072 or more), the bin is treated as empty and excluded from coverage. In this case,
VCS issues a warning. Any cross bins that reference this bin are also excluded.
Coverage Support for Inconsequential Code Reduction
This feature allows you to enable Inconsequential Code Reduction (ICR) optimization with
coverage. After ICR optimization is enabled, the coverage report displays the redundant
signal as Unreachable(Optimized).
