2. Defining the tenure and enabling the data collection.
In the Xbus example, if you want to measure the transaction throughput performance
(i.e for the XBUS transfers), associate the tenure with the Xbus transaction. To denote
the starting and ending of the tenure, define two additional events in the XBUS Master
Driver (started, ended). started is triggered when the driver obtains a transaction
from the sequencer. ended is triggered once the transaction is driven on the bus and
the driver is about to indicate seq_item_port.item_done(rsp);. At the same time,
if started is triggered, a callback is invoked to get the PAN to start collecting the
statistics.
// run phase
virtual task run_phase(uvm_phase phase);
get_and_drive();
reset_signals();
join
endtask : run_phase

// get_and_drive
virtual protected task get_and_drive();
@(negedge xsi.sig_reset);
forever begin
@(posedge xsi.sig_clock);
seq_item_port.get_next_item(req);
respond_to_transfer(req);
seq_item_port.item_done();

end
endtask : get_and_drive
