Avoid advancing simulation time based on time value read from the TEXTIO file
(Example 19). This style leads to an inefficient testbench as the vector file controls the
amount of time to advance. Usually your vector file contains more than one line per clock.
This might be efficient only when your vector file contains waits for several clocks before
advancing time. Example 20 shows the wait for time statement as the recommended
coding style for reading and applying vectors.

