Return values
The access functions return 0 on success or 1 on error. You can use vhpi_chk_error()
immediately after the call to check the following errors:
• Not a valid object: the object designated by the handler does not carry a value or is
NULL.
• Bad format: the given format is inappropriate for the subtype of the object, or has not
been set.

