Releasing Objects on Hold
The interface provides the vhpi_release_hold() function to release the value assigned
to an object. This value must have been assigned using the vhpi_put_value() function
with either the vhpiForceHold or vhpiForceHoldPropagate flag.
int vhpi_release_hold(vhpiHandleT h);
The function returns 0 on performing a successful release, or returns 1 if the object does
not have a value placed on hold.
Scheduling a Transaction
You can use the vhpi_schedule_transaction() function to schedule a transaction on
a VHPI object’s driver. The transaction can be scheduled with zero or non-zero delay and
with inertial or transport mode.

