C Initialization Function
Write the C initialization function to perform the following tasks:
1. Gets a handle for first the input port of the nand gate (port1).
2. Gets a handle for second the input port of the nand gate (port2).
3. Gets a handle for the output port of the nand gate (port3).
4. Allocates value data structure for each port and specifies the format of the data to be
read and written to the value data structure. Since the input and the output ports for the
nand gate are of type std_logic, the format is specified as vhpiEnumVal.
5. Reads the initial value of the input ports, evaluates the output port (using the
eval_nand2() routine), and then writes back the value of the output port.

2-Input Nand Gate (NAND2)
6. Allocates a callback data structure for each of the input ports and fills in the fields with
the required data. The callback reason is vhpiCbValueChange on that input port.
7. Registers the callbacks so each callback triggers everytime there is a change of value
on its particular input port.
When either callback fires, it calls the callback function that in turns calls the evaluation
function that has the functionality of the nand gate. The callback function then compares
the new value of the output with the old value and if they are different, it writes back to the
output port.
The complete C code for the initialization function is as follows:
