+newTimingcheckMsg
By default, a timestamp in a timing violation message is printed with the timescale
module. It can be controlled by the user through the $timeformat option. The
+newTimingcheckMsg runtime option enables VCS to print timestamps in simulation
precision when a timing violation occurs.
Simulation precision is the smallest time precision across a design. It is not affected by the
$timeformat() specified by the user, nor by the time unit specified for various modules.
This option also displays the time unit along with the number, thereby making the violation
messages clear.
